      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fenton_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Fenton was platted on April 21, 1899 by the Western Town Lot Company along the Fox Lake branch of the Chicago and North Western Railway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fenton_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early economy focused on farming, with German and Norwegian settlers forming the Holtz colony in 1870, emphasizing cattle raising.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fenton_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Gentle till plains and shallow depressions around Fenton create microclimates that slightly vary moisture retention and frost patterns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/fenton_iowa"
    },
    {
